% Intrapulmonary Percussive Ventilation System: LCD L33786 and its Policy
% Article A52495 (DME MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it
% includes dmepos.le (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need,
% refills) and decides the claims for an intrapulmonary percussive
% ventilation system (E0481). The LCD has one coverage statement and it is
% a denial: "An intrapulmonary percussive ventilator (IPV) (E0481) has not
% been demonstrated to be reasonable and necessary in the home setting. It
% will be denied as not medically necessary." The claim is within the scope
% of the model and within the durable medical equipment benefit (Policy
% Article A52495), and it fails the question whatever its record and its
% documentation show.
%
% How the denial is written. The one rule of the question states it as an
% exclusion: a claim of this policy is reasonable and necessary only if its
% item is not an intrapulmonary percussive ventilation system — and E0481,
% the policy's only code, is one. No claim passes; the rule is there so that
% the checklist of a failed claim reads "question failed" (the coverage
% question is what the LCD decides) rather than blaming the payment
% conditions, and so that an explanation points at the LCD's sentence. The
% record has no facts to state: no criterion reads one, and no finding is
% consulted — an unrecorded finding would leave the answer conditional,
% where the LCD is categorical.
%
% Not modelled: the coding guidelines of the Policy Article (E0481 includes
% the compressor, the hand held units, the tubing and the accessories — a
% claim for those separately is incorrect coding, a matter of coding rather
% than of coverage).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % derived
    *an item* is an intrapulmonary percussive ventilation system.

the knowledge base ipv includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base ipv includes:

LCD L33786 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33786".
the text of LCD L33786 is at "sources/lcd/L33786.txt".
Policy Article A52495 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52495".
the text of Policy Article A52495 is at "sources/article/A52495.txt".

% What the system is (the Policy Article's coding guidelines).
rule ipv_system with provenance Policy Article A52495,
        confer "E0481 includes the compressor, hand held units, tubing and all related accessories":
an item is an intrapulmonary percussive ventilation system
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0481".

section applicability is:

% The Policy Article states no documentation requirement of its own beyond
% the general ones of dmepos.le.
ipv has no specific documentation requirements.

% The code this policy decides, and its benefit: durable medical equipment
% (Policy Article A52495).
rule ipv_codes with provenance Policy Article A52495,
        confer "Intrapulmonary Percussive Ventilation Systems are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is ipv
    if the code is in ["E0481"].

rule ipv_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52495,
        confer "Intrapulmonary Percussive Ventilation Systems are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is ipv.

section question is:

% No claim for an intrapulmonary percussive ventilation system is reasonable
% and necessary. The exclusion below is how the denial is stated (see the
% header): the only code of the policy is the system's, so no claim of the
% policy satisfies it.
rule ipv_denied with provenance LCD L33786,
        confer "An intrapulmonary percussive ventilator (IPV) (E0481) has not been demonstrated to be reasonable and necessary in the home setting":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the policy of the claim is ipv
    and it is not the case that
        the item is an intrapulmonary percussive ventilation system.
